From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Fri, 11 Feb 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: no prompt, no card move and no control change for a
 seat that is not alive at n > 2

With more than two duelists, an eliminated seat could still get a prompt
and could still get a card on its field. The lib functions give the folded
value 0 to the core as a real seat. These guards stop the effect in the core.
Every change is in an n > 2 branch. With two duelists the code is the same.

field.h: new is_skipped_seat(p). It is true with n > 2 when p is not alive.

playerop.cpp: a skipped seat gets no message. The core answers for it at
step 0 with the stock "no choice" answer. Idle and battle commands end the
phase. Yes/no and option give 0. Card, unselect, sort and position choices
take the simple-AI answer. Chain gives -1 (0 if forced). Tribute and sum give
an empty list. Announce choices take the first value. Place choices use the
first living seat when the chooser is not alive.

operations.cpp: MoveToField fails like a full zone when the field owner is not
alive. When the chooser is not alive, the owner of the field chooses.
GetControl does not move a card to a seat that is not alive.

card.cpp: a control effect that names a seat that is not alive is ignored.
It left a card in one mzone list with the controller of another seat.

The nduel future checks eliminated-prompt (22 runs) and eliminated-cards
(3 runs) are now 0. The stuck-prompt failures are gone. n3 is 20 of 20
and n4 is 20 of 20. win-consistency in Tag is a harness count error.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UrYy4jjEcbJHKdcVYasfdb
